Willard Richards</a> begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside>Job Smith says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83514\">50 cents, 100 B,</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83515\">John Green says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83516\">50 cents, 100 B</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83517\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"3415343543153222714\"><a href=\"#3415343543153222714\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per1420\" person=\"per1420\" title=\"R. T. Madison\">Robert Madison</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Madison, R. T.\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/r-t-madison\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside> Says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83518\">300 brick. $150</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83519\">Willam Wood say</td> <td xml:id=\"X83520\">25 ct — 50 brick</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83521\">Frideric Cook says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83522\">$1.50= 300 brick</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83523\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6430733907971280419\"><a href=\"#6430733907971280419\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans8\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> handwriting ends; handwriting presumably of subscriber begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside>Elisha Barton</td> <td xml:id=\"X83525\">2,00 C Paid<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4641661054078045743\"><a href=\"#4641661054078045743\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans9\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a>.</p><hr></div></div></aside></td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83527\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13479916291832971406\"><a href=\"#13479916291832971406\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans10\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Handwriting presumably of subscriber ends; <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside>Mrs Orson Spencer<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6042825040073873577\"><a href=\"#6042825040073873577\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans6\"><span id=\"documenttrans6\">6</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Catherine Curtis Spencer. (Orson Spencer, “Obituary,” <span class=\"title\">Millennial Star,</span> 15 Feb. 1847, 60.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\"> <span class=\"title\">Latter-day Saints’ Millennial Star.</span> Manchester, England, 1840–1842; Liverpool, 1842–1932; London, 1932–1970. </p></div></div></div></aside> Says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83530\">100 lbs flour at Laws Mill<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10463874214869898311\"><a href=\"#10463874214869898311\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans7\"><span id=\"documenttrans7\">7</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/william-law\" class=\"referenceInPop\">William Law</a> and <a href=\"/person/wilson-law\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Wilson Law</a> operated a combined sawmill and flour mill on the <a href=\"/place/mississippi-river\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Mississippi River</a> at Sidney Street, between Locust and Marion streets. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/trustees-land-book-b-4-august-1842-8-december-1845/268\" class=\"externalLink\">Wilson Law, Purchase Record, 24 Jan. 1842, Trustees Land Book B, Galland Purchase, 266–267 [insert]</a>, <a href=\"/paper-summary/trustees-land-book-b-4-august-1842-8-december-1845/278\" class=\"externalLink\">275</a>; Notice, <span class=\"title\">Wasp,</span> 11 June 1842, [2]; “Weather, Wind and Works,” <span class=\"title\">Wasp,</span> 17 Sept. 1842, [2]; see also <a href=\"/paper-summary/deed-to-wilson-law-24-january-1842-as-recorded-in-hancock-county-deeds\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/deed-to-wilson-law-24-january-1842-as-recorded-in-hancock-county-deeds\" poptitle=\"Deed to Wilson Law, 24 January 1842, as Recorded in Hancock County Deeds\">Hancock Co., IL, Deed Records, 24 Jan. 1842, vol. K, pp. 490</a>–<a href=\"/paper-summary/deed-to-william-law-24-january-1842\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/deed-to-william-law-24-january-1842\" poptitle=\"Deed to William Law, 24 January 1842\">492</a>, microfilm 954,599, U.S. and Canada Record Collection, FHL.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\"> <span class=\"title\">The Wasp.</span> Nauvoo, IL. Apr. 1842–Apr. 1843. </p></div></div></div></aside></td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83534\">Aug. 3. John Miller</td> <td xml:id=\"X83535\">order— 50 cts.—</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83536\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13172436378693270795\"><a href=\"#13172436378693270795\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans11\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> handwriting ends; handwriting presumably of subscribers begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13847309956718907438\"><a href=\"#13847309956718907438\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x114254\" person=\"x114254\" title=\"Henry Hoagland\">Henry Hoagland</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Hoagland, Henry\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/henry-hoagland\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside></td> <td xml:id=\"X83538\">2 days Brick laying</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83539\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"12943805348921772594\"><a href=\"#12943805348921772594\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x91071\" person=\"x91071\" title=\"George Colemere\">George Colemere</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Colemere, George\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/george-colemere\">View Full Bio</a></p></div></div></aside></td> <td xml:id=\"X83540\">2 days \" \"</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83541\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1266259724816587523\"><a href=\"#1266259724816587523\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per1372\" person=\"per1372\" title=\"George Philander Stiles\">Geo. P. Stiles</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Stiles, George Philander\"><p>18 July 1816–Sept. 1885. Attorney, judge, politician. Born in Watertown, Jefferson Co., New York. Son of John Stiles and Persis Cole. Moved to Le Ray, Jefferson Co., by 1820. Moved to Pamela, Jefferson Co., by 1830. Married first Julian Mackemer, 7 Nov. 1841...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/george-philander-stiles\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside></td> <td xml:id=\"X83542\">$5. Laying Brick</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83543\">Sam<span class=\"underscore\">el</span>. M. Marr</td> <td xml:id=\"X83544\">$4. Labor</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83545\">Jacob Baum</td> <td xml:id=\"X83546\">1. C</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83547\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10236209019269737207\"><a href=\"#10236209019269737207\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans12\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Handwriting presumably of subscribers ends; <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"2441642649934565532\"><a href=\"#2441642649934565532\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per1110\" person=\"per1110\" title=\"Arthur Morrison\">Arthur Morrison</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Morrison, Arthur\"><p>Ca. 1802–after 1850. Merchant, tailor, militia captain, judge. Born in Virginia. Moved to Batavia, Clermont Co., Ohio, by 1825. Married Keziah Ann Voriz, 17 Nov. 1825, in Clermont Co. Moved to Palestine, Darke Co., Ohio, by 1830. Baptized into Church of Jesus...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/arthur-morrison\">View Full Bio</a></div></div></aside> says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83549\">sheeting for the house</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83550\">Thomas Richardson say</td> <td xml:id=\"X83551\">3 days wrok—</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83552\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"739196956160922137\"><a href=\"#739196956160922137\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans13\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> handwriting ends; handwriting presumably of subscriber begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside>William Nixon</td> <td xml:id=\"X83554\">300— Brick</td> </tr> </tbody></table> <div class=\"noindent wasptag\"> [p. 4]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><table width=\"100%\"> <tbody><tr> <td xml:id=\"X83513\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"8415656449674068708\"><a href=\"#8415656449674068708\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans7\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Handwriting presumably of subscribers ends; <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside>Job Smith says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83514\">50 cents, 100 B,</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83515\">John Green says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83516\">50 cents, 100 B</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X83517\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6573966526452679755\"><a href=\"#6573966526452679755\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"per1420\" person=\"per1420\" title=\"R. T. Madison\">Robert Madison</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Madison, R. T.\"><p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/person/r-t-madison\">View Full Bio</a></p