=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Handwriting presumably of subscriber ends; <a href=\"/person/willard-richards\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Willard Richards</a> begins.</p><hr></div></div></aside>Mrs Orson Spencer<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7649228467853659781\"><a href=\"#7649228467853659781\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans6\"><span id=\"documenttrans6\">6</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Catherine Curtis Spencer. (Orson Spencer, “Obituary,” <span class=\"title\">Millennial Star,</span> 15 Feb. 1847, 60.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\"> <span class=\"title\">Latter-day Saints’ Millennial Star.</span> Manchester, England, 1840–1842; Liverpool, 1842–1932; London, 1932–1970. </p></div></div></div></aside> Says</td> <td xml:id=\"X83530\">100 lbs flour at Laws Mill<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6564383425790494294\"><a href=\"#6564383425790494294\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans7\"><span id=\"documenttrans7\">7</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\"><a href=\"/person/william-law\" class=\"referenceInPop\">William Law</a> and <a href=\"/person/wilson-law\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Wilson Law</a> operated a combined sawmill and flour mill on the <a href=\"/place/mississippi-river\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Mississippi River</a> at Sidney Street, between Locust and Marion streets. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/trustees-land-book-b-4-august-1842-8-december-1845/268\" class=\"externalLink\">Wilson Law, Purchase Record, 24 Jan. 1842, Trustees Land Book B, Galland Purchase, 266–267 [insert]</a>, <a href=\"/paper-summary/trustees-land-book-b-4-august-1842-8-december-1845/278\" class=\"